{"title":"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram shown, David begins at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and walks in a straight line to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and then walks in a straight line from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. Cindy also begins at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and walks in a straight line to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>How much farther does David walk than Cindy?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/f/c5fdf3629d630b3f8eb7f2d0303077a6c0c0357d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 0 \\text{ m} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 2 \\text{ m} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 4 \\text{ m} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 6 \\text{ m} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 7 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"448\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/b/d3b4bf9a4b02a953f591f345bbe2271c34915905.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 8 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/1/3d195591e04c0117f36441dcc6e879bb01e21d15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB = 15 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"93\" height=\"14\" />, so David walked <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/4/d4477cdd8a6c31488aaa538b9fca6e5dcf09df19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 + 15 = 23 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"113\" height=\"15\" /> in total.\n</p><p>Next, using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Pythagorean theorem\">Pythagorean theorem</a>, we can find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> (the distance that Cindy walked):\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9b667c35ab4170a2919f350a32c1d7114689471.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB^{2} = AC^{2} + CB^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/5/be582b97f6f97910447aea03802680d625959219.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB^{2} = 8^{2} + 15^{2} = 64 + 225$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"218\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/9/2a9b19487f77c8b019704cf6a982b955ab8c5ff9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB^{2} = 289$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"89\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/8/708965ffed1308ac233683c40bbef189f9a97bc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = \\sqrt{289} = 17 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"159\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Since David walked <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b91e871c04ad36cb76be28614ffb925bdb2287e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" /> and Cindy walked <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d698626ff05f1f0559387b798d00633b8af0146.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" />, David walked <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/e/faef8430958d345fd1b0f451dd2b0a40efc439a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23 - 17 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 6 \\text{ m}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"160\" height=\"30\" /> farther\n</p><p>~anabel.disher \n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2